doins oracle case: nodie-eapi3

Isolates helpers that cannot die (EAPI 3, no --helpers_can_die) on the
same install_dir failure as die-eapi8: real logs "install_dir failed."
with a traceback and continues, rc 0. At EAPI <= 6 the wrapper reads
the legacy INSDESTTREE instead of __E_INSDESTTREE (hence
INSDESTTREE=/usr/lib/probe in env and no --preserve_symlinks /
--helpers_can_die in args).
If the native port regressed to dying here, rc.txt would read 1.

Run exactly as an install phase runs it (bin/ebuild-helpers/doins):
  cd <SRC> && env -i <env> doins -r tree
with <env> from the checked-in env file (placeholders @ED@ @T@
@DISTDIR@ @CHECKOUT@ @PYSHIM@ substituted with the stage trees,
empty value unset), PORTAGE_PYTHON pointing at the argv-logging
shim (see the header), and the checked-in manifests materialised
by doins/materialise.py (source mtimes pinned, so -p is stable).
File contents are recorded as size + sha256 (out of scope for
chmod-lite, in scope here per D3); symlink modes are always ----.
args holds the exact doins.py argv after the script path, one
element per line as raw bytes (`\\` for backslash, `\n` for
newline; <SCRATCH>/<CHECKOUT> substituted, newins tmpdir suffix
as newins.RAND). stdout.txt exists only when non-empty.

Provenance (D4):
  portage-ref: portage-3.0.82.2
  portage-commit: 1d95fc2c552a2c7d347e54093fa0e5b172a57004 (3rdparty/repos.toml [portage] commit)
  python: Python 3.14.8 (/usr/bin/python)
  uid: 1000, umask: 022 (enforced)
  staging: tmpfs (raw non-UTF-8 names OK: yes)
  xattr-fs: user.* xattrs work on tmpfs
  generator-locale: LANG=C.utf8 (enforced); charmap=UTF-8
  date: 2026-10-09 (UTC day granularity; the only field that may change
    between regenerations)
  scrub: <SCRATCH>/<CHECKOUT> in args/stderr/stdout; newins.RAND
  root-vs-user: identical
